{"duration_api_ms":239374,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"caaabe0a-8063-4a9a-b28c-4bb516685237","total_cost_usd":0.283122,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12357,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":23369,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17624},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12357,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":23369,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12357},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":23369,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12357,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.283122,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":17624,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Only 1 of 16 feasible designs is non-dominated (C-ea2223901bd4: 295k W/m2, 396.2 K). The normalised hypervolume of 0.316 is almost entirely set by bondline temperature: reference span is 150 K and about 0.0059 of hypervolume is gained per kelvin, versus about 0.0014 per 10k W/m2 of flux. Temperature falls with larger D, higher bluntness and cone angle, and steeper entry. Feasibility is capped by max_g (about 12, reached near gamma -3.6) and by heatshield mass fraction (margin near zero at D of about 3.35). Bluntness of 1.25 with cone of 70 deg, and B=1.2 with cone 69 at D=3.0, returned extrapolation failures. Low cone angles at high bluntness return invalid geometry.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-94a9f7a46f9b (D3.2, B1.2, c69.5, -3.8) reaches 392.2 K but max_g is 12.309, so it is infeasible. C-1618bda1fac0 at -3.7 gives 12.139. This implies about 1.7 g per degree and a gamma limit near -3.6 at D of about 3.2.\",\"g at fixed gamma rises about 0.45 per metre of D. C-ea2223901bd4 (D3.3, -3.4) gives 11.686 and C-963d4cdbada1 (D3.2, -3.5) gives 11.816. This supports about -3.55 as the limit at D of about 3.3.\",\"Temperature falls about 2.2 K per 0.1 m of D. C-c0f89c462bd0 (D3.1) is 400.8 K and C-963d4cdbada1 (D3.2) is 398.0 K at the same gamma. C-7ef0b45caabb (D3.1) is 398.4 K and C-2b74a3ea4aeb (D3.0) is 399.2 K.\",\"Mass-fraction margin shrinks about 0.06 per 0.1 m of D. It is 0.209 at D3.0 (C-2b74a3ea4aeb), 0.097 at D3.2 (C-1618bda1fac0) and 0.035 at D3.3 (C-ea2223901bd4). C-f84c59a3cc23 at D3.34 has 0.010. D of about 3.36 is therefore near the limit.\",\"B/cone effect: C-94a9f7a46f9b (B1.2, c69.5) is about 1.4 K cooler and about 7k lower in flux than C-1618bda1fac0 (B1.0, c66), after correcting for gamma.\",\"Shallower gamma lowers flux slightly but raises temperature about 1 K per 0.1 deg. C-d2c4b79f3796 (-3.3) is 402.9 K and C-2b74a3ea4aeb (-3.6) is 399.2 K, at similar D.\",\"Extrapolation failures: C-40f2342796ee (3.0,1.2,69), C-0202524b57fd (2.6,1.25,70) and C-1d24bfa5f84e (2.8,1.25,70). C-94a9f7a46f9b (3.2,1.2,69.5) evaluated fine, so B of 1.2 at cone 69.5 is the edge of the known-safe region.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Heat flux and bondline temperature both fall as ballistic coefficient falls and effective nose radius rises. Larger D, higher B and larger cone angle all do this, since drag coefficient and nose radius grow. Steeper entry shortens the heat pulse and lowers temperature, but raises peak g. The optimum is therefore pinned at three corners at once: D near the mass-fraction limit (about 3.35), gamma near the g limit (about -3.5 to -3.6), and B/cone near the edge of the aero-surrogate hull (B1.1-1.2, cone 67-69.5). This is largely inferred from the 40 rows, with standard entry-heating physics only as background. The simple additive sensitivities I use are local linear fits and may be off near the constraint edges.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The margins on max_g (about 0.003 to 0.02) and mass fraction (about 0 to 0.05) are within my model error, so several proposals near the edge may come back infeasible. Hull behaviour for B of 1.2 or more is unclear because it may depend on D. The effect of gamma on the mass fraction is not separated from the effect of D. The shallow-gamma flux gain is extrapolated from few points.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"Same geometry as the 392 K design but with gamma moved to just inside the g limit. Expected g is about 11.955.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.59},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Anchors the g limit at D=3.2 and gives a feasible point cooler than the current front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly larger D lowers temperature and flux. gamma is relaxed to hold g near 11.92.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Intermediate point along the D ramp toward the mass-fraction limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.3 with the best-known B/cone and gamma backed off to -3.55 to offset the D-dependent g rise.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Likely dominates C-ea2223901bd4 on both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"Safer-g variant of the previous design, with gamma at -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":291500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Robust feasible point that probably dominates the current front member.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.34 gives more temperature gain from D while the mass-fraction margin is still expected positive (about 0.02).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests how much the mass-fraction limit binds at high cone angle.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"Pushes D toward the mass-fraction limit (expected margin about 0.01).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":283000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the D edge for feasibility, which sets the coldest attainable bondline.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"Boundary probe on D. Mass-fraction margin is predicted to be about zero.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":281000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Brackets the mass-fraction limit. If feasible it is the coldest point yet.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ea2223901bd4\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate B/cone (1.1/67, inside the proven hull) at D 3.3 and gamma -3.55, to check that a lower-risk aero setting still beats the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":67.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates the effect of B/cone from D and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ea2223901bd4\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate B/cone between the proven points (1.1/67 and 1.2/69.5).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills in the B/cone trend and checks hull coverage between known points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4976b56437f4\",\"rationale\":\"Uses the proven B1.1/c67 aero setting at D 3.33 and gamma -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.33,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Low-risk high-D feasible point with a robust hull.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower gamma at large D trades some temperature for lower flux and low g.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":280200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front toward lower flux and may still dominate C-ea2223901bd4.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"Low-flux end of the trade-off. g is low and the mass-fraction margin is unchanged from the D 3.34 case.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests how flux scales at shallower gamma. It is a coverage point for the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ea2223901bd4\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the hull edge at B1.25 and cone 70 with D 3.3, larger than in the earlier failures (D 2.6 and 2.8).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Determines whether the extrapolation failure depends on D. It could unlock a further B gain.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"Same B/cone probe as the previous proposal at D 3.2, where B1.2/c69.5 is known to work.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":298000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the hull edge close to a proven point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ea2223901bd4\",\"rationale\":\"Keep B at 0.95 and raise cone to 69.5 to isolate the cone effect from bluntness.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates the B and cone contributions for later modelling. It may return a hull failure.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"Fine step in D between 3.3 and 3.34 with gamma -3.52.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.32,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.52},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Dense sampling near the predicted optimum.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4976b56437f4\",\"rationale\":\"High D with B1.15/c68.5, which is a slightly milder aero setting than the edge.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.48},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the mass-fraction margin at D 3.36 holds with a slightly lower cone angle.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.28 with gamma -3.53, giving a small g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.28,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":291500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills in the D-gamma trade-off with a likely-feasible point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-94a9f7a46f9b\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.36 with gamma -3.53 to balance the g and mass-fraction limits.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":283800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether both limits can be near-active at once.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ea2223901bd4\",\"rationale\":\"Keeps B at 1.2 but drops cone to 66 to measure cone sensitivity at high B, with D 3.3 and gamma -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":292000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests cone sensitivity and the risk of invalid geometry at B1.2 with a smaller cone.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":192156,"type":"result","duration_ms":239414,"uuid":"6056944b-3ea1-418d-ab7b-50574fcdc6e6","ttft_stream_ms":1205,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1205,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
